1
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:11,120
Turn on the lights in the room and try stepping back,
would you?

2
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:24,280
Anyone who's broke, come to my place.

3
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:29,020
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

4
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:32,800
Look at that blue sky.

5
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:36,300
White clouds.

6
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:07,380
Snow Country Police Box

7
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:28,180
Even though it's March,
there's so much snow!

8
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:31,460
At this rate, no matter how much we shovel,
we'll never keep up.

9
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,700
Ugh, this snow is in the way!

10
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:37,280
Yes!

11
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:39,440
Senpai! Good morning!

12
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:41,951
But it's really piled up.

13
00:01:42,001 --> 00:01:44,120
That must be rough for the town.

14
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:47,077
Yes. Tokyo drivers aren't used to snow,

15
00:01:47,127 --> 00:01:49,840
and it sounds like accidents
are happening everywhere.

16
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:52,260
I see. With snow like this,

17
00:01:52,310 --> 00:01:54,480
it's a good thing public
transport isn't running.

18
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:55,260
Urgh!

19
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:56,520
W-who's there!

20
00:01:56,940 --> 00:01:59,080
Ryo-chan. Were you over there all along?

21
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:02,440
Don't "were you there" me.
Check properly before you drop it.

22
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:05,880
You idiot!
You show up late and still talk big!

23
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:12,620
If you've got all that energy to waste,
go do something useful for people for once.

24
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:20,720
Hey, what's that supposed to mean? With this snow,
go help the townspeople get where they're going. Yeah, yeah, got it.

25
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:22,600
Me.

26
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:49,580
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee...

27
00:02:49,580 --> 00:02:51,120
Heh-heh, strike!

28
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:53,180
Hey, you guys!

29
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:54,740
Backbeh!

30
00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:56,220
Spank your butts!

31
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:58,900
Damn it! Get back here!

32
00:02:59,040 --> 00:02:59,640
Whoa!

33
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:02,740
Come and get me!

34
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:03,700
Get back here!

35
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:05,620
Yes!

36
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:06,880
Total success!

37
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:08,180
You bastards!

38
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:12,520
Damn it, just you wait!

39
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:17,140
Leave the other side just as it is,

40
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:20,720
if I dig a pitfall here,
those guys will fall right into it.

41
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:24,600
Right, it's done.

42
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:29,040
If I do say so myself,
it's a pitfall of superb quality.

43
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,640
Oho, you've really worked hard at it.

44
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:34,320
Well, of course.
If someone does it to me, I do it back.

45
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:37,780
I've lived that way since I was a kid,

46
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:38,920
Alright!

47
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,440
Da-bu, Chief!

48
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:43,960
You haven't shoveled any snow,
you've just been up to nonsense all day!

49
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:45,980
W-what are you talking about?

50
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:49,220
I was just carrying it here.

51
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:53,040
Please, help me!

52
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:56,060
You brought it on yourself.

53
00:03:56,060 --> 00:03:57,940
You idiot!

54
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:01,060
What do you think you're doing?

55
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:04,780
A guy like you should stay buried
down there for the rest of your life.

56
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:05,900
Please, stop it!

57
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:07,840
This is going too far with the horseplay!

58
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:10,200
Just kidding.

59
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:13,120
Your hands haven't stopped moving at all,
have they?

60
00:04:19,540 --> 00:04:22,000
Patrol's over, just got back.

61
00:04:22,620 --> 00:04:23,480
Good work.

62
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:24,660
Thanks for your hard work.

63
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:26,220
It's started snowing again.

64
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:28,840
Yeah, it looks like it'll
pile up again tonight.

65
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:30,580
Good work.

66
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:32,820
Yes, nothing unusual to report.

67
00:04:34,380 --> 00:04:37,760
But pulling a night shift on a day like this,
poor Ryo-chan.

68
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:41,080
Shut up, you don't really think I'm pitiful.

69
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:42,700
I'm stuck with you until morning.

70
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:44,160
Bee-da.

71
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:46,620
If I had to be with Ryo-chan
on a day like this...

72
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:50,300
I'd just get stuck making meals,
"make this, make that."

73
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:52,380
Damn, she read me.

74
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:56,020
Well, just chalk it up
to bad luck and give up.

75
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:56,800
Excuse me.

76
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:58,060
See you.

77
00:04:58,620 --> 00:04:59,220
Damn it.

78
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:03,940
This is turning into a real snowstorm,
let's hurry and head home.

79
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:06,740
Honestly, what a heartless bunch you are.

80
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:10,480
Well then, Ryo-san, I've got to go,
my train leaves at 8:05.

81
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:11,800
Wait.

82
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:13,600
What is it, Ryo-san?

83
00:05:14,020 --> 00:05:16,860
It takes three hours from
here to your place, right?

84
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:21,240
So if you don't hurry,
you won't make the last train.

85
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:23,085
I told you to wait.

86
00:05:23,135 --> 00:05:25,720
You're overlooking something important.

87
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:27,759
Say you get on the train now,

88
00:05:27,809 --> 00:05:30,600
what will you do if it
stops running halfway?

89
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:32,220
W-what? No way.

90
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:35,798
You'll be trapped in
the snow with your train,

91
00:05:35,848 --> 00:05:38,220
and no one will rescue you until morning.

92
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:40,840
The power will go out,
the heater will stop working,

93
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:43,100
and you'll freeze to death.

94
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:45,320
Poor thing.

95
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:46,260
No way...

96
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:48,880
It's already eight o'clock.

97
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:51,880
We won't make the last train now.

98
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:53,200
That's cruel, Ryo-san.

99
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:57,680
So you'll keep me company
until morning, right?

100
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:00,560
Ryo-sama

101
00:06:01,260 --> 00:06:02,140
Maria

102
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:04,860
I heard you're on the night shift tonight,
Ryo-sama,

103
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:06,800
so I went and brought you some treats.

104
00:06:08,220 --> 00:06:09,000
Welcome!

105
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:11,160
Is Terai-san with you too?

106
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:12,660
Well...

107
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:13,331
In that case,

108
00:06:13,381 --> 00:06:17,280
let's have a fun hotpot party tonight!

109
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:19,480
Hotpot! That sounds great!

110
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:23,820
Ohoho! This meat looks delicious!

111
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:27,040
Ryo-san, please stop poking at it!

112
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:31,000
Sorry, sorry. I know, let's call Honda too!

113
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:34,140
Honda

114
00:06:34,140 --> 00:06:37,280
Actually,
there's a girl who really wants to meet you,

115
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:38,380
and she's here at the police box.

116
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:39,540
Who?

117
00:06:39,540 --> 00:06:42,480
Squishy, smooth, and curvy as can be.

118
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:44,240
So will you be late,
or are you coming right away?

119
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:45,160
We're waiting for you.

120
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:48,340
Alright, that makes four of us, right?

121
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:51,100
With this many, we should have a fun night.

122
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:55,620
We apologize for the inconvenience.

123
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:57,380
Due to an incident ahead

124
00:06:57,380 --> 00:07:00,300
the train is currently stopped because
of a river accident caused by the snow.

125
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,260
Please wait a little longer.

126
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:06,160
It was a lie?

127
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:08,400
That's cruel, senpai.

128
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:11,420
I rushed through this snow to get here,
you know.

129
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:13,060
It's not a lie!

130
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:13,940
See?

131
00:07:13,940 --> 00:07:16,560
What's the big deal about that meat?

132
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:20,400
It's the tender, silky, plump meat of
a female cow, all springy and smooth!

133
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:22,600
Just a moment ago, it was "Honda, eat it!"

134
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:25,320
It sounded like it was saying that in a seductive voice,
I swear.

135
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:28,280
Please stop messing around, seriously!

136
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:29,480
I'm going home.

137
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,160
Won't you stay and eat?

138
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:33,180
No, thank you!

139
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:35,940
Honestly, you have no sense of humor.

140
00:07:35,940 --> 00:07:38,320
Don't come crying later asking to eat,
you know.

141
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:41,640
Ryo-san, there's no way we'd eat beef,
no matter what.

142
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:43,980
I thought it was funny.

143
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:45,300
S-senpai...

144
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:49,220
Something's going on outside,
and it's a big deal!

145
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:52,160
So come on, let's stay and eat.

146
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:53,960
Let's eat!

147
00:07:57,120 --> 00:08:00,040
The heavy snowfall that hit the
Kameari area of Katsushika Ward

148
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,120
has exceeded one meter,
and damage is starting to appear everywhere.

149
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:05,560
Yes, this is Katsushika Police Station.

150
00:08:06,780 --> 00:08:08,660
Houses collapsed in the 3-chome area?

151
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:11,120
Understood. We'll rush there immediately.

152
00:08:11,780 --> 00:08:14,620
Oh no, they say there's an
avalanche on the slope in 2-chome.

153
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:18,080
Hah, we can't handle
this with just us anymore.

154
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:20,767
We just got word from headquarters.

155
00:08:20,817 --> 00:08:22,600
This is an emergency
notice for all officers.

156
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:24,300
Understood.

157
00:08:29,220 --> 00:08:30,280
Come on, Honda.

158
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:31,700
Hurry up and draw.

159
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:33,000
Mm...

160
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:35,880
Then this one...

161
00:08:35,880 --> 00:08:37,400
Heh heh heh.

162
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:38,780
Fiyah!

163
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:42,360
A-ah, speaking of which,
the other day on my motorcycle -

164
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:46,040
Honda, changing the subject all of a sudden.
What's the matter?

165
00:08:46,460 --> 00:08:48,280
It's nothing, really.

166
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:50,420
There are awful people in this world.

167
00:08:50,420 --> 00:08:52,740
The other day, on the seat of my motorcycle,

168
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:54,820
someone left a bag of garbage.

169
00:08:54,820 --> 00:08:56,340
And it was kitchen waste,

170
00:08:56,340 --> 00:08:59,340
Ugh... th-that's terrible, isn't it?

171
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:02,435
Speaking of that,

172
00:09:02,485 --> 00:09:07,480
the manju I put in the fridge the
other day has mysteriously disappeared.

173
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:10,660
And I was saving it to share with Ryo-sama!

174
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:12,920
W-wow, that's terrible.

175
00:09:13,860 --> 00:09:18,000
Come to think of it, a package my
parents sent me from home went missing too.

176
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:19,300
Whaaaaaat!

177
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:20,640
What's wrong, Honda?

178
00:09:20,820 --> 00:09:23,807
No, I just mean,
what a terrible person there is out there.

179
00:09:23,857 --> 00:09:25,100
Ha ha Right?

180
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:25,812
Honestly,

181
00:09:25,862 --> 00:09:29,600
the four of us should make sure
we never become people like that.

182
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:33,520
Even Ryo-san says something
sensible once in a while.

183
00:09:33,920 --> 00:09:35,440
"Once in a while" is unnecessary.

184
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,560
Residents,

185
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:56,980
the weight of the snow may
cause houses to collapse.

186
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:58,880
Snow vehicles are now
making their rounds, so

187
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:00,420
please calmly evacuate.

188
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:02,860
Chief,

189
00:10:03,380 --> 00:10:05,760
How is the evacuation going in Nakagawa?

190
00:10:05,760 --> 00:10:09,280
It's going smoothly. Everyone should
be evacuated in about thirty minutes.

191
00:10:09,780 --> 00:10:13,100
I see. By the way,
I don't see Ryotsu anywhere.

192
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:16,740
Komachi and the others have
called the police box many times,

193
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:18,160
but no one answered.

194
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:21,900
Knowing him,
he probably slipped out to goof off.

195
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:24,640
That lazy good-for-nothing never changes.

196
00:10:29,860 --> 00:10:32,300
Yay, I knocked everyone down!

197
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:35,820
That's not fair, senpai,
collecting that many pillows!

198
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:39,320
Yeah, why do you have so many pillows?

199
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:42,780
But it reminds me of pillow
fights on school trips.

200
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:46,060
Yeah, it brought back childhood memories.
It was fun.

201
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:49,740
Right? Okay, what should we play next?

202
00:10:49,740 --> 00:10:52,260
We're still playing something?

203
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:55,220
Of course! We're playing
until we're completely worn out!

204
00:11:09,520 --> 00:11:13,060
Whoa, it's pitch black.
Did I wake up too early?

205
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:16,820
It's already past eight.
Still, it's really dark.

206
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:21,480
Hey, that's strange... it's a power outage.

207
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:27,020
It won't open. What's wrong?

208
00:11:27,340 --> 00:11:29,720
The lights won't turn on,
and the windows won't open either.

209
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:33,320
That's odd... It's still the middle of the night,
so what's the problem?

210
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:36,540
Sorry, but it's already
past eight in the morning.

211
00:11:36,540 --> 00:11:39,460
Yeah, that's strange.

212
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:09,740
Nothing at all. Not a peep.

213
00:12:09,740 --> 00:12:10,620
Damn it.

214
00:12:12,140 --> 00:12:13,520
Not even a drop of water comes out, damn it.

215
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:15,960
The water pipes must have frozen or burst.

216
00:12:16,780 --> 00:12:18,240
My cell phone won't connect either.

217
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:19,420
What should we do?

218
00:12:19,420 --> 00:12:21,700
We're completely cut off.

219
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:24,960
I never expected it to pile up
this much while we were sleeping.

220
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:27,520
What on earth are we supposed to do?

221
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:32,220
The heavy snowfall that hit
the Kameari area last night

222
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:34,840
has become a record-breaking
snowstorm for Tokyo,

223
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:37,120
with snow depths exceeding five meters.

224
00:12:38,020 --> 00:12:41,340
Oddly, this heavy snow is
limited to the Kameari area alone.

225
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:48,280
At this rate, we can't tell
at all what's going on outside.

226
00:12:48,280 --> 00:12:51,560
Anyway, I'll dig through the
snow and go check on things.

227
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,300
Leave it to you, Ryo-san.

228
00:12:53,300 --> 00:12:55,780
Senpai, please hurry and go get help.

229
00:12:56,460 --> 00:12:57,740
We're counting on you.

230
00:12:58,160 --> 00:12:59,400
Alright, I'm going.

231
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:05,640
It's no good, the door won't budge at all.

232
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:07,500
You two, give me a hand.

233
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:08,900
O-okay, got it.

234
00:13:14,220 --> 00:13:15,020
What is it?

235
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:17,400
Ryo-sama, please close the door.

236
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:18,900
Hurry.

237
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:19,720
What?

238
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:22,760
It stopped.

239
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:26,180
Maybe right now this police box

240
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:28,300
is standing on an
incredibly delicate balance,

241
00:13:28,300 --> 00:13:30,260
and that's why it's still safe.

242
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:32,580
In other words, the snow's weight

243
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:34,920
is evenly distributed
across the entire building,

244
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:36,660
so the police box is barely

245
00:13:38,020 --> 00:13:45,080
holding up. But if we open the door, that balance will break,
and the building won't be able to bear the weight.

246
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:53,180
We'll be crushed! Hell, we're completely cut off and can't even escape!
Damn it! What do we do?

247
00:13:53,180 --> 00:14:00,980
Oh my, this is terrible. Issuing the
evacuation advisory early was the right call.

248
00:14:00,980 --> 00:14:04,000
We never expected five meters of snow.

249
00:14:05,060 --> 00:14:07,920
Nakagawa, you take charge of
the snowplows and heavy equipment

250
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:09,720
and clear the snow from the streets.

251
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:10,700
Understood.

252
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:13,600
Reiko, check whether anyone was left behind

253
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:15,060
and patrol the streets.

254
00:14:15,420 --> 00:14:16,000
Roger.

255
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:21,840
Where on earth is Ryotsu?

256
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:23,520
Even at a time like this, he's late.

257
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,460
Brr, it's cold.

258
00:14:28,460 --> 00:14:30,980
Senpai,
shouldn't we just turn on the heater?

259
00:14:31,420 --> 00:14:34,900
Idiot! If we turn on a
stove in a sealed place,

260
00:14:34,950 --> 00:14:36,520
we'll run out of oxygen!

261
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:39,500
But at this rate, we'll freeze to death!

262
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:41,840
Well, I'm... I'm fine...

263
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:43,860
Hey! Don't sleep! If you sleep, you'll die!

264
00:14:44,180 --> 00:14:46,260
I'm feeling so... sleepy too...

265
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:48,340
Mr. Terai, wake up! Hang in there!

266
00:14:48,780 --> 00:14:50,320
Hey! Honda! Don't sleep!

267
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:52,420
Mr. Terai! Hang in there!

268
00:14:52,420 --> 00:14:53,640
Don't sleep! Don't die!

269
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:54,780
No! Don't sleep!

270
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:55,320
Here!

271
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:03,360
So the area next to
Kameari got no snow at all?

272
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:04,580
Looks that way.

273
00:15:06,220 --> 00:15:08,740
Here you go. There's still more.

274
00:15:08,740 --> 00:15:10,700
Reiko, thank you for your hard work.

275
00:15:10,700 --> 00:15:12,060
We'll take over now.

276
00:15:12,060 --> 00:15:13,940
Thanks, that's a big help.

277
00:15:13,940 --> 00:15:17,540
Reiko, did you happen to see Maria?

278
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:20,320
No, she didn't come here.

279
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:24,060
I see. We haven't been able
to reach her since last night.

280
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:29,740
Never mind Ryotsu,
but Honda and Terai didn't go home either.

281
00:15:29,740 --> 00:15:31,500
I wonder what happened.

282
00:15:35,580 --> 00:15:40,820
The drowsiness is gone,
but for some reason my face keeps throbbing.

283
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:43,700
It's just your imagination.

284
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:44,360
Do you think so?

285
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:46,980
I'm starving.

286
00:15:46,980 --> 00:15:51,180
If I'd known, I should've
saved some of yesterday's hotpot.

287
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:54,760
And we used up all the
ingredients we brought.

288
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,913
Yakiniku, nabeyaki udon,

289
00:15:56,963 --> 00:15:59,720
I want to eat curry ramen.

290
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:03,840
Stop! Thinking about it makes
it even harder to hold out.

291
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:08,640
What's wrong?

292
00:16:08,980 --> 00:16:11,100
N-nothing.

293
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:13,960
Suspicious.

294
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:16,100
Terai, take off the blanket.

295
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:17,840
W-why?

296
00:16:17,980 --> 00:16:19,340
Just lower the blanket.

297
00:16:19,340 --> 00:16:20,480
It's cold, isn't it?

298
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:23,220
It's chocolate!

299
00:16:23,220 --> 00:16:27,000
Terai-san, how awful,
you were going to eat it all by yourself!

300
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,160
No, I only just noticed it.

301
00:16:29,160 --> 00:16:34,280
As punishment for being so noisy, I won't let you have this chocolate.
I'll eat it myself instead.

302
00:16:34,640 --> 00:16:35,880
Senpai, that's not fair.

303
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:38,880
That's right,
we should divide it fairly among everyone.

304
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:40,880
Yeah, it was mine to begin with.

305
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:45,080
What are you saying? As long as things like this exist,
petty fights will keep going on.

306
00:16:45,080 --> 00:16:48,460
That's why I'll take responsibility
and dispose of it for you.

307
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:49,240
I'll eat some too.

308
00:16:50,100 --> 00:16:50,820
Me too.

309
00:16:52,600 --> 00:17:17,460
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts!
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts! It hurts!

310
00:17:26,940 --> 00:17:30,020
For now, please dump the snow we
collected from the streets here.

311
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:35,240
But even if we gather all the snow in town,
I doubt the park space alone will be enough.

312
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:40,960
Wait, that's the utility pole
in front of the police box.

313
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:44,660
So that means... no way, no way, senpai?

314
00:17:45,460 --> 00:17:48,800
All that wasted energy
has made me even hungrier.

315
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:52,640
No one's coming to help us.
Are we just going to die like this?

316
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:54,140
Yeah, right?

317
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,500
If we have to die,
I'd at least like to go without any regrets.

318
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:02,680
Honda, I'm sorry. It was my fault.

319
00:18:02,680 --> 00:18:04,720
What's gotten into you all of a sudden?

320
00:18:04,720 --> 00:18:09,100
The one who put the garbage bag on Honda's bike,
the one you were talking about yesterday, was me.

321
00:18:09,100 --> 00:18:10,960
Why?

322
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:15,760
I'm sorry, it was me who ate Maria's manju.

323
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:20,160
It looked so delicious that I couldn't
resist and ate it without asking.

324
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:21,540
I'm sorry.

325
00:18:22,540 --> 00:18:26,280
Actually, it was me who opened
Terai's package without permission.

326
00:18:27,180 --> 00:18:28,160
That's...

327
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:32,080
Yes, I opened it by mistake
without checking the sender's name.

328
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:34,320
I'm really sorry.

329
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:37,400
Anyone can make a mistake like that.

330
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:40,280
That's right, anyone can have
a momentary lapse of judgment.

331
00:18:41,220 --> 00:18:43,620
Then you'll forgive me too?

332
00:18:43,620 --> 00:18:45,060
Of course.

333
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:48,800
Honestly, I'm not really
bothered about the garbage either.

334
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:49,700
Honda.

335
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:50,560
Maria.

336
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:51,340
Terai.

337
00:18:51,340 --> 00:18:52,280
I'm sorry.

338
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:57,800
Isn't it wonderful?
Sharing the truth deepens our friendship.

339
00:18:58,160 --> 00:18:58,840
Ryo-san

340
00:18:59,780 --> 00:19:04,980
Now that I think about it, wasn't it you, senpai,
who said we should open Terai-san's package?

341
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:09,620
Come to think of it, who was it that
said we could eat the manju in the fridge?

342
00:19:09,620 --> 00:19:10,940
It was Ryo-san, wasn't it?

343
00:19:10,940 --> 00:19:12,900
W-was it?

344
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:16,960
That time too,
when we went out to eat with Lord Ryo,

345
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:18,560
I was about to go throw out the garbage,

346
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:22,500
That's right, we didn't have time, so Ryotsu
said to just leave it on Honda's bike for now.

347
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:24,460
and that I'd clean it up later.

348
00:19:24,460 --> 00:19:26,800
N-no way, was that really how it went?

349
00:19:29,340 --> 00:19:31,860
Calm down, everyone, keep your cool!

350
00:19:31,860 --> 00:19:33,660
Cool your heads with this.

351
00:19:37,620 --> 00:19:40,900
Damn it, how can we just sit around
waiting for rescue in such a dangerous place?

352
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:43,560
If that's the case,
we're getting out of here all at once.

353
00:19:45,340 --> 00:19:46,920
So the police box is down there

354
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:49,260
Is Ryotsu really in there?

355
00:19:49,720 --> 00:19:52,200
Yes, Ryo apparently hasn't gone home either,

356
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:54,320
so he's probably still buried in the snow.

357
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:57,180
Maria-chan also hasn't been
reachable since yesterday,

358
00:19:57,180 --> 00:19:58,400
Komachi-chan said.

359
00:19:58,780 --> 00:19:59,880
Maybe...

360
00:19:59,880 --> 00:20:02,640
If Terai and Honda can't
be reached either, then...

361
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:04,520
They're probably together, most likely.

362
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:08,860
The weight of the snow could
make the police box collapse.

363
00:20:09,340 --> 00:20:10,400
Ryo-tsu...

364
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:15,160
Listen!
I'll open the door alone, all at once,

365
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:19,120
then dig straight through the snow and
escape before the police box collapses!

366
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:20,180
Roger!

367
00:20:20,520 --> 00:20:21,460
Right, let's go!

368
00:20:21,740 --> 00:20:22,280
Yeah!

369
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:23,780
Go!

370
00:20:26,760 --> 00:20:28,180
W-what's wrong?

371
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:31,160
Uh-oh! It's collapsing!

372
00:20:39,620 --> 00:20:40,200
Ryo-chan!

373
00:20:41,700 --> 00:20:42,500
The Chief!

374
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:45,520
Now we have nowhere to go back to!

375
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:48,080
The only way left is to
dig up to the surface!

376
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:54,780
Are you okay, Ryotsu?

377
00:20:55,920 --> 00:20:58,800
Guys like you can stay buried
there for the rest of your lives!

378
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:00,400
Ryotsu...

379
00:21:03,380 --> 00:21:06,860
The snow piled up to
about three or four meters!

380
00:21:06,860 --> 00:21:10,220
We should be out by now, so what's going on?

381
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:13,560
Ryo-sama,
let's try digging in a different direction.

382
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:18,740
Yeah, maybe there's an
unusually heavy pile of snow here.

383
00:21:18,740 --> 00:21:20,360
Alright, then this way!

384
00:21:25,620 --> 00:21:28,120
No matter how far we dig,
it's nothing but snow.

385
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:30,300
How many meters of snow has piled up?

386
00:21:30,300 --> 00:21:33,500
It's hopeless.
The whole world must be covered in snow.

387
00:21:33,980 --> 00:21:35,520
We're going to die here.

388
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:39,180
Don't say that!
We'll definitely get out of this!

389
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:41,160
I'm not dying in a place like this!

390
00:21:41,540 --> 00:21:43,940
If it comes to this,
we'll keep digging upward nonstop!

391
00:21:45,360 --> 00:21:47,260
Where are you? Answer me!

392
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:49,300
Terai! Honda!

393
00:21:49,900 --> 00:21:50,880
Maria!

394
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:55,160
Up! Up!

395
00:21:55,300 --> 00:21:57,140
Since it's come to this,
aim for somewhere up there!

396
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:01,360
The senior officers aren't here, are they?

397
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:03,700
Let's search around too.

398
00:22:03,700 --> 00:22:04,040
Yes.

399
00:22:04,040 --> 00:22:07,620
Hey, look! It's getting bright.
We're outside!

400
00:22:10,320 --> 00:22:13,040
We're out! We did it, we're saved!

401
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:15,200
What is this height?

402
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:17,880
The Chief and the others are over there!

403
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:19,080
Bē-chan

404
00:22:20,600 --> 00:22:21,680
Ryotsu!

405
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:23,380
Why is he all the way up there?

406
00:22:23,380 --> 00:22:26,360
That Bakabon, making us worry like this!

407
00:22:26,360 --> 00:22:29,300
Chief, you were that worried about me?

408
00:22:29,300 --> 00:22:31,340
Bē-chan!

409
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:33,880
Kei-chan, what's that sound?

410
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:35,960
Chief!

411
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:37,880
Good for you, Honda.

412
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:40,360
Thank goodness the whole
world isn't buried in snow.

413
00:22:40,360 --> 00:22:40,740
Yes.

414
00:22:40,740 --> 00:22:43,920
Ryo-san,
hasn't it been shaking this whole time?

415
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:47,060
Well, we're this high up,
of course it's going to shake.

416
00:22:47,060 --> 00:22:49,680
Ryo-sama, something's wrong down below.

417
00:22:49,680 --> 00:22:52,940
Everyone's moving away from us somehow.

418
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:58,760
Ryo, can you hear me? The rescue team is on its way,
so just stay put right there.

419
00:22:59,220 --> 00:23:02,580
What did you say? Please say it louder!

420
00:23:03,160 --> 00:23:05,280
No, don't shout!

421
00:23:06,180 --> 00:23:07,560
What?

422
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:11,420
I said, if you shout, the snow will...

423
00:23:11,420 --> 00:23:14,980
I can't hear you at all!
Please say it louder!

424
00:23:16,020 --> 00:23:19,500
I said, if you shout,
it'll trigger an avalanche!

425
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:20,400
Hey!

426
00:23:22,100 --> 00:23:23,140
Chief, watch out!

427
00:23:23,820 --> 00:23:24,780
Whoa!

428
00:23:44,480 --> 00:23:46,040
I thought I was going to die.

429
00:23:46,700 --> 00:23:47,900
Hey, Ryotsu!

430
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:49,380
C-Chief!

431
00:23:49,900 --> 00:23:53,160
How much more trouble do you have to cause before you're satisfied,
you wretch?

432
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:56,300
Someone like you should stay buried
in the snow for the rest of your life.

433
00:23:56,880 --> 00:24:03,420
That's not fair! It's not my fault!
Chief! Please help us!

434
00:24:11,560 --> 00:24:16,260
Why is that? Why is that?
Why is that? Why is that?

435
00:24:16,440 --> 00:24:18,420
Ryo-san's... why is that?

436
00:24:19,920 --> 00:24:25,000
Why do Ryo-san's eyebrows
look like black seagulls?

437
00:24:26,300 --> 00:24:31,460
Why can he run so fast in sandals?

438
00:24:31,460 --> 00:24:33,200
Why?

439
00:24:33,940 --> 00:24:39,360
Why does Ryo-san always
have his sleeves rolled up?

440
00:24:39,360 --> 00:24:40,620
Why?

441
00:24:40,980 --> 00:24:45,740
Why is he so wild and yet
everyone looks up to him?

442
00:24:46,260 --> 00:24:47,860
Why?

443
00:24:48,740 --> 00:24:51,660
It doesn't really matter, but

444
00:24:52,840 --> 00:24:58,360
Why is this anime's title so long?

445
00:24:59,040 --> 00:25:01,180
Kochira Katsushika-ku Kameari
Kōen-mae Hashutsujo makes its debut!

446
00:25:01,180 --> 00:25:02,880
I wonder why.

447
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:05,360
I wonder why.

448
00:25:07,080 --> 00:25:08,640
I wonder why.

449
00:25:08,640 --> 00:25:09,740
I wonder why.

450
00:25:09,740 --> 00:25:11,100
I wonder why.

451
00:25:12,580 --> 00:25:14,060
I wonder why.

452
00:25:14,060 --> 00:25:15,440
I wonder why.

453
00:25:15,440 --> 00:25:16,300
I wonder why.

454
00:25:16,300 --> 00:25:16,640
Why?

455
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:17,380
Why?

456
00:25:17,380 --> 00:25:18,080
Why?

457
00:25:18,080 --> 00:25:19,000
I wonder why.

458
00:25:29,880 --> 00:25:31,060
What is it, Electrode Old Man?

459
00:25:31,060 --> 00:25:32,880
Another sales pitch for a new product?

460
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:36,260
A car with autopilot linked to the car navigation,
they say.

461
00:25:36,260 --> 00:25:37,480
Sounds interesting.

462
00:25:37,480 --> 00:25:38,780
Let me take a ride in it, just a little.

463
00:25:38,780 --> 00:25:40,200
Where has this car been driving?

464
00:25:40,200 --> 00:25:41,540
And it won't stop!

465
00:25:41,540 --> 00:25:43,800
Surely it's not a defective product?

466
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:46,840
Next time: where are we, Electrode Old Man?

467
00:25:47,240 --> 00:25:47,800
Nice to meet you.

468
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:50,900
That's Kameari.

469
00:25:51,940 --> 00:25:54,280
Well, surely it's Kameari.

470
00:25:55,540 --> 00:25:59,260
Everybody, come on over to our town!

471
00:26:00,420 --> 00:26:00,860
Thank you.

